# Every call that can write or erase the MCU flash: file, enclosing function, symbol, count.
# test_flash_paths.sh compares this with the firmware. A difference fails the test.
#
# Before you add a row: can this run while a motor is active? If so it must go through
# odrive_bridge_flash_begin() and _end(), and test_flash_paths.sh must check that path.
# `sh test_flash_paths.sh --print` lists the current state.

# ---- At runtime, through commands. Every entry below asks the flash guard ------------------------

# sys.save, sys.eetest, sys.eedump, sys.eeformat
Odrive-Wheel/src/cmd_table.cpp - ffb_eedump 1
Odrive-Wheel/src/cmd_table.cpp - ffb_eeformat 1
Odrive-Wheel/src/cmd_table.cpp - ffb_eetest 1
